# Web UI (`peaky serve`)

Serve-only product: **on-demand** viewsheds, links, and preset edits over `core/` + splatter.

## Do

- **Reuse `core/`** — `load_preset`, `preset_to_request`, viewshed workspace digests, `run_viewshed_coverage`.
- **Cache layout** — `<preset>/.peaky/cache/viewsheds/<digest>/`.
- **Keep HTTP thin** — routes in `serve/app.py`; logic in `serve/*.py`.

## Avoid

- Reimplementing splatter or preset parsing in handlers.
- Batch-all-sites on page load when one overlay was requested.
- Web-only tunables that belong in preset YAML.
- **`wa-callout` + `hidden` alone** — the danger variant still renders an empty bar. Toggle errors with the `hidden` attribute **and** CSS `wa-dialog wa-callout[hidden] { display: none !important; }` (see `app.css`). Clear `textContent` when hiding.
- **Modal scroll** — one scroll container per dialog (`::part(body)`). No nested `overflow-y: auto` panes inside modals (double scrollbars). Stack map + form vertically when side-by-side feels cramped.

See skill `peaky-serve` and MEMORY.md.
